# Line endings have ONE owner: git, at the boundary.
#
# The clone is one of many writers (2026-07-15) — cloud Anna commits from a
# Linux runner, Andrew's laptop is Windows. Every JSON writer in scripts/ uses
# text mode without newline="", so Python translates \n on write and a Windows
# state write flips the WHOLE file: one 2026-07-27 close produced 6871 changed
# lines in lexicon.json with zero content change, and would have conflicted
# line-for-line with the next cloud write.
#
# Normalising here rather than passing newline="\n" at nine call sites is the
# same argument as quiet hours moving into push_to_phone (2026-07-26): four
# copies of a rule and one gap, and the gap is the lane that fires. This covers
# every writer, including the ones not written yet.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Audio and images are bytes; never let the filter touch them.
*.mp3 binary
*.jpg binary
*.png binary
